  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Advanced ACT Math includes combinations, permutations, compound probability, and normal distribution concepts.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Permutations",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( _nP_r=\\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Combinations",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\binom{n}{r}=\\dfrac{n!}{r!(n-r)!} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Bayes (simple)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( P(A|B)=\\dfrac{P(B|A)P(A)}{P(B)} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Expected value",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( E=\\sum x_i P(x_i) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 8.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "How many 3-letter arrangements (order matters) can be made from the word MATH? \\[ _4P_3=\\frac{4!}{1!}=24. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Counting, Expected Value & Normal Distribution",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Fundamental counting principle:</strong> \\(m \\times n\\) ways for two independent events. <strong>Expected value:</strong> \\(E(X) = \\sum x_i P(x_i)\\). <strong>Standard normal:</strong> \\(z = \\dfrac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}\\); about 68% of data within \\(1\\sigma\\), 95% within \\(2\\sigma\\), 99.7% within \\(3\\sigma\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Expected value",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A game pays $8 if you roll a 6 on a fair die, and you lose $2 otherwise. What is the expected gain per roll? <p>\\(E = 8 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{6} + (-2) \\cdot \\dfrac{5}{6} = \\dfrac{8-10}{6} = -\\dfrac{2}{6} \\approx -\\$0.33\\).</p><p>The game is unfair — you lose on average 33 cents per roll.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "In a class of 30, 18 play football (F), 14 play basketball (B), and 6 play both. How many play neither sport?",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(|F \\cup B| = 18+14-6 = 26\\). Neither \\(= 30-26 = 4\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
